        "notes": "Line 1 (passes: 1, author sourcing, 2026-10-14): all three pages fetched. The claim is that Seollal is the Lunar New Year and that 새해 복 많이 받으세요 is a common greeting then. Encyclopedia of Korean Culture, 설: the definition names it the first day of the lunar year, the same as 설날; the 세시풍속 section calls 새해 복 많이 받으십시오 a modern New Year greeting, so the note says 'common' and never 'traditional'. Encyclopedia of Korean Culture, 인사, item ⑤: the Seollal greeting 새해에 복 많이 받으십시오. National Institute of Korean Language column: 새해 복 많이 받으십시오 is a suitable New Year greeting; the bow itself greets, so no line in the cell is said during a bow (no bow is shown). The cell uses the polite 해요체 form 받으세요 (the cell's register); the formal 받으십시오 of the sources is the same wish. The note says 'a common greeting', names no group as a whole and copies no wording (English note, Korean locators). Carried by: q3 intro Hoya line, q3 Discover page 1 caption, q3 blurb."
